1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,680
The first thing that I would do on my self development journey is I would stop perceiving things as easy or hard.
在个人成长的路上，我首先会停止把事情看成简单或困难。

2
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:11,279
I feel like the way you think about things in your life really changes the way that you approach them and how you handle them.
我觉得，你看待生活中事情的方式，确实会改变你面对和处理它们的方式。

3
00:00:11,279 --> 00:00:17,520
So if you stop looking at doing things as easy and hard and you start looking at them as more of just decisions.
所以，不再把做事分成简单或困难，而把它们更多地看作选择。

4
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:25,120
Decisions that either lead to what you want or what you don't want it makes it that much easier to get over the mental hurdle of doing something that you may or may not want to do.
这些选择会带你走向或远离你想要的结果，这样就更容易跨过做某件事时的心理障碍。

5
00:00:25,120 --> 00:00:29,600
We do this so much in life we'll be like that's hard that's easy and we start putting these labels on things and.
生活中我们经常这样，说这很难、那很简单，然后给事情贴标签。

6
00:00:29,600 --> 00:00:34,319
Once you start putting on labels in your mind automatically there's going to be a barrier to entry.
一旦开始贴标签，脑中就会自动出现一道进入的门槛。

7
00:00:34,319 --> 00:00:40,800
So take away easy and hard and just say that they are simply decisions towards or away from the things that you want.
因此，拿掉简单和困难这两个标签，只把它们看成走向或远离目标的选择。

8
00:00:40,800 --> 00:00:45,600
The second thing that I would do in this month is I would give myself one month to read one book.
这个月我会做的第二件事，是给自己一个月读完一本书。

9
00:00:45,600 --> 00:00:52,870
What reading does is it develops your mind it develops your vocabulary it is stimulating for the brain and it also gives you a sense of accomplishment.
她说，阅读能发展思维和词汇，刺激大脑，还会带来成就感。

10
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:56,560
Once you finish that one thing which will help you with your confidence in the future.
当你完成一件事之后，这份成就感也会帮助你建立未来的信心。

11
00:00:56,560 --> 00:01:05,840
So reading one book it can be easy or hard it can be developmental or fictional obviously if it's self developmental you are going to be killing two birds with one stone.
所以，读的书可简单可难，可谈成长也可为小说；如果是自我成长类，她认为就能一举两得。

12
00:01:05,840 --> 00:01:11,279
I love developmental books that don't feel like developmental books and some suggestions that I have for you.
我喜欢那种不像成长书的成长书，我也有一些书想推荐给你们。

13
00:01:11,279 --> 00:01:19,679
Would be the alchemist actually I have them right here the alchemist or the four agreements um anything really by paulo qualo he has many amazing books.
比如《牧羊少年奇幻之旅》，其实就在这里；还有《四个约定》，以及保罗的其他作品，她说他的书都很棒。

14
00:01:19,679 --> 00:01:25,439
But the alchemist would definitely be the first most important book on that list or think like a monk by j shetty.
不过《牧羊少年奇幻之旅》肯定是书单上的首选；或者字幕中 j shetty 所写的《像僧人一样思考》。

15
00:01:25,439 --> 00:01:32,000
These are all really great developmental books that don't necessarily feel boring or mundane my number one pick is going to be the alchemist.
这些都是很好的成长书，不一定让人觉得无聊或乏味。我的第一选择是《牧羊少年奇幻之旅》。

16
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:38,159
This is a story about a boy and it's like the journey through life about finding your life's purpose it is such an easy read and.
这是关于一个男孩的故事，像是在讲寻找人生目的的旅程；它很容易读下去。

17
00:01:38,159 --> 00:01:42,720
Once you read it you're just going to be like you're going to want to start working on yourself to get to exactly what you want to do.
她说，读完以后，你会想开始改善自己，走向自己真正想做的事。

18
00:01:42,720 --> 00:01:46,400
Because we really only have one life so I would give yourself one month to read one book.
因为人生只有一次，所以我会给自己一个月读完一本书。

19
00:01:46,400 --> 00:01:52,240
Because there are so many benefits that you get from reading that anything else can't really give you the same experience.
她认为阅读益处很多，其他事情很难带来相同的体验。

20
00:01:52,240 --> 00:01:57,519
The third thing that I would do is I would stop thinking that I have to live life like everybody else.
我会做的第三件事，是不再认为自己必须像其他所有人那样生活。

21
00:01:57,519 --> 00:02:08,880
I feel like there's so much group think in life especially if you come from a a parents in an area specific areas where everybody does things the same way because they've always done it that way.
我觉得生活里有很多从众思维，尤其在某些家庭或地区，大家只因为一直如此，就做一样的事。

22
00:02:08,880 --> 00:02:12,400
I think that is one of the most dangerous mindsets that we can have as people.
我认为，这是我们可能抱有的最危险的思维方式之一。

23
00:02:12,400 --> 00:02:20,400
And not everyone has family members or friends that help them break from this group think and that is why I'm here because I'm here to break you from the group think.
不是每个人都有家人或朋友帮助自己摆脱从众思维，所以我在这里，就是想帮助你们打破这种从众思维。

24
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:24,159
I think one thing that I really value in life is thinking like an individual.
我在生活中非常看重的一点，是像独立的个体一样思考。

25
00:02:24,159 --> 00:02:31,519
And what this does is breaking away from group think allows you to grow it allows you to change what you wear the way you talk the things that you're into.
摆脱从众思维会让你成长，允许你改变穿着、说话方式和兴趣。

26
00:02:31,519 --> 00:02:37,040
And it stops making you feel like you have to do it the same way that everyone else before you has done it.
这样你就不会再觉得，自己必须沿用前人做事的方式。

27
00:02:37,040 --> 00:02:41,280
This even works in the workplace there are such mentalities that you can adopt being in the workplace.
这在职场也适用；人在工作环境里可能形成某些思维方式。

28
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:49,600
Just because someone did it like that before you doesn't mean it's the most effective doesn't mean it's the most transformational and doesn't mean it's the most efficient for anybody.
别人以前这样做，不代表这种做法最有效、最能带来改变，也不代表对任何人来说都最高效。

29
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:56,079
So break through from the group think and really start thinking as yourself if your friends want to go out late and you want to wake up early.
所以，打破从众思维，真正以自己的立场思考。朋友想玩到很晚，而你想早起——

30
00:02:56,079 --> 00:03:03,120
You don't go out with your friends late you're breaking from the group think and thinking that you have to do the same exact thing as everyone all the time.
那你就不和朋友玩到很晚；这是摆脱从众思维，不再觉得时时刻刻都要和别人一样。

31
00:03:03,120 --> 00:03:08,960
If your friends and your parents and whatever your family dress like this and you want to start changing the way that you're dressing.
如果朋友、父母或家人都穿某种风格，而你想开始改变自己的穿着——

32
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:14,400
You need to start breaking away from the group think because the way you want to dress is going to get you to where you want to be.
你需要开始摆脱从众思维，因为她认为你想要的穿着方式能带你走向目标。

33
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:17,280
You have to be really comfortable with breaking from that mentality.
你必须能坦然面对摆脱那种思维方式这件事。

34
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:25,040
And with breaking from that mentality obviously you're opening yourself up from feedback from the people that you love the workplace the friends whatever it may be.
打破那种思维，也意味着你会听到来自所爱的人、工作环境或朋友等各方面的反馈。

35
00:03:25,040 --> 00:03:32,480
But breaking from that group think will be so beneficial for you not only on your self development journey but also on your corporate journey or also in your family life as well.
但她认为，摆脱从众思维不仅有益于个人成长，也会有益于职业发展和家庭生活。
